  "brief": "LONA briefing  2026-11-02 03:41 UTC\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nWHAT THE RULES DID\r\n  Funding is trending: XPL down 3 days to +10.95%.\r\n      A single day of funding moving is noise. A run of days is a position being built or unwound, and it is what decides whether a carry leg is getting richer or being crowded out from under you.\r\n      XPL.funding_annual.streak = -3  ·  XPL.funding_annual = +10.95%\r\n  The carry book got thinner: mean yield moved -1861.5 bp since yesterday.\r\n      Still gross of the hedge. Finding 012 showed this number is only worth what the spot leg costs to hold.\r\n      carry.mean_yield.change_1d = -1861.5 bp  ·  carry.mean_yield = +22.47%\r\n\r\nCONTEXT\r\n  No market in the universe is at a new 50-day high.\r\n      The correct book is 100% cash, which is the rule working rather than failing - it sits out about a third of all days by design.\r\n      breakout.count = 0  ·  universe.size = 20\r\n  Fully in cash.\r\n      breakout.deployed = 0%\r\n  Carry book is 4 legs at +22.47% a year, gross.\r\n      That is what funding pays, not what the trade returns. Finding 012 showed the same yield turning negative once the spot hedge is charged for, so this number is only worth what the hedge is worth. Nothing here has measured this account's actual borrow cost or basis slippage.\r\n      carry.legs = 4  ·  carry.mean_yield = +22.47%\r\n  Fear and Greed reads 37 - fear.\r\n      Recorded for later testing. LONA has not established that this index predicts anything, so it informs no rule.\r\n      sentiment.fear_greed = 37\r\n  Biggest moves in the universe since yesterday: XPL -14.26%.\r\n      XPL.mark.move_1d = -14.26%\r\n",
